 ## Overview
-The Mohr Diagram is a visualization technique for stress tensors that plots normal stress against shear stress to represent the most important invariants [S1, book]. It sets itself apart from scalar volume rendering by explicitly mapping the relationship between the three eigenvalues of a symmetric tensor to geometric circles, allowing for the inspection of maximum shear stress and the transition between tensile and compressive forces [S1, book]. It builds on [Shape Space (Tensor Eigenvalue Space)](8885-shape-space-tensor-eigenvalue-space.md) by projecting tensor invariants onto a 2D plane.
